ed a very real threat thanos  did this by winning in infinity war he  did this by killing loki and destroying  the hulk this was the pinch point so how  does kang prove himself well kang will  do this by killing ant-man this will be  the next pinch point in the mcu now  let's talk about kang first and how i  believe that many people really aren't  prepared for just how insanely awesome  this villain is going to be to start it  off king has basically millions of  variants kevin feige even confirmed this  he said that we are going to see many  different versions of kang many  different variants of kang and basically  it's not just going to be one kang that  the avengers are going to have to fight  although i do believe that there will be  one superior kang but here's the deal in  the comics kang essentially has a  limitless number of variants and he's  actually able to transfer his  consciousness into another variant right  before he dies essentially making him  immortal which alone makes him a huge  threat but make no mistake kang is worse  than thanos in fact kang let thanos do  everything that he did or i should say  he who remains who is a variant of kang  the conqueror nathaniel richards he let  thanos do everything because he  controlled the tva which controlled  everything in loki season 1 they even  state that the tva let them do  everything they let the avengers go back  in time they said that was supposed to  happen meaning he who remains let that  happen he who remains king is such a  boss that he let thanos eliminate half  of the universe he didn't care because  he knew the ending he knew that the  avengers would go back in time and  defeat him he knew everything which is  what makes him so dangerous but it gets  even worse he who remains wasn't even  really evil but king king the conqueror  is very evil and he who remains even  says if you think i'm evil wait till you  meet my variants well guess what  if you think i'm  evil  well this way  till you meet 